				<section class="faq" aria-labelledby="faq">
					<h2 id="faq">FAQ</h2>
					<h3>Does claude --resume work after copying the transcript?</h3>
					<p>Yes, if the transcript sits in the project folder Claude Code expects for the directory you run it in, and the paths inside it point at that directory. Run claude --resume &lt;session-id&gt; from the project folder on the new machine.</p>
					<h3>Do I need to commit before moving a session?</h3>
					<p>Not with Zoes. It packs uncommitted and untracked files into a temporary commit, and lays them back on the host as uncommitted changes. Files your .gitignore excludes stay behind. By hand, you need some way to carry them: a WIP commit you undo on the server, or a copy of the files.</p>
					<h3>Does it work for Codex?</h3>
					<p>Yes. Codex keeps each conversation as a rollout JSONL file under ~/.codex/sessions. Zoes carries Claude Code and Codex conversations. For other agents it moves the code and starts a fresh session from a summary.</p>
					<h3>Is the session on my Mac deleted?</h3>
					<p>No. Zoes never closes the Mac session. Once the handoff is done, the host has its own copy of the conversation, and the Mac session reads as before. If a step fails, the Mac session is still there.</p>
					<h3>What OS can the host run?</h3>
					<p>Zoes hosts can run macOS, Linux or Windows, on arm64 or amd64. The handoff runs git and sh on the host and builds Unix paths, so use a macOS or Linux host for it.</p>
				</section>
